00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.540
So how are microservices
revolutionizing

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:54.890
app development?

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:58.040
Along with the rise of
cloud computing and Agile,

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.200
the increasing use
of microservices

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:04.640
has profoundly affected how
enterprises develop software.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:08.750
Microservices enable
businesses to innovate faster.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.610
Development teams
can independently

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:13.070
develop, deploy,
and scale components

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:15.260
of large applications.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:19.700
The adoption of cloud
containers and CI/CD tools

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:23.660
has made microservices
implementations much easier,

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:26.630
leading to more and more
modern software being built

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:29.270
as a set of microservices.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:31.460
App development teams
implement microservices

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:35.810
using a variety of stacks like
Kubernetes and Netflix OSS,

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:37.560
depending on their needs.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.010
And all of these
microservices use web APIs

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:42.020
as a mechanism to
communicate with one another.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:49.890
So both the concept of an API
and the concept of microservice

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:52.570
involve structure and
interactions of software.

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:54.720
A microservice can
be misconstrued

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.570
as simply an end point
to provide an API,

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:00.720
but microservices have much more
flexibility and capabilities

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:01.650
than that.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:03.180
An easy way to
think about an API

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:06.960
is it's basically a contract
of actions you can request

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.970
for a particular service.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:11.160
APIs are in use
today in a multitude

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:14.750
of web apps such as social
media, banking, telco,

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:17.100
health care, and many more.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.800
The standardized contract
allows for external apps

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.603
to interface with one another.

00:03:22.603 --> 00:03:24.270
In today's world eight
codes are usually

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.460
developed using RESTful style.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:28.830
These APIs have
a series of verbs

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:32.460
associated with HTTP actions
like get, post, and put.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:38.860
So the Apigee API platform
enables enterprises

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:42.310
to accelerate innovation,
provide shared services

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:46.810
and data, and adapt to
market and customer needs.

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:50.710
APIs have become the foundation
of that fast-moving digital

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:52.330
